# OpenCode iOS port patch -- 0001
# Title: iOS Node build target, non-SEA iOS prelude / asset set / http shim
# Upstream: anomalyco/opencode @ e8238bae9b807b72ecfc75afd3a9fe2e6b07b944 (v2.2.5)
# Files: packages/cli/src/node/target.ts
#        packages/cli/script/build-node.ts
#        packages/cli/script/node-assets.ts
#        packages/cli/vite.node.config.ts
# Why: upstream's Node distribution build targets Node 26 SEA on desktop platforms. The
#      iPhoneOS runtime is Node 22.9: it has no module.registerHooks, its node:sea exposes
#      no getAssetKeys/getRawAsset, WebAssembly is disabled, and no desktop Node addons
#      exist for iOS. The generated bundle must start from stock Node builtins only (no
#      SEA prelude, no registerHooks, no node:sea import) and must not ship macOS
#      dylibs/addons or helper executables that cannot load on the device.
#      The iOS prelude also declares the installed assets dir, OPENCODE_IOS=1 and the
#      rootless /var/jb PATH prefixes. @effect/platform-node's strictContentLength is
#      disabled for iOS because Node 22.9 stores the raw Content-Length header string and
#      throws ERR_HTTP_CONTENT_LENGTH_MISMATCH on otherwise-correct responses (fixed in
#      later Node lines). Photon's wasm module is kept external/lazy (WebAssembly is off).
# Test: OPENCODE_TARGET=ios-arm64 OPENCODE_IOS=1 bun run script/build-node.ts --bundle-only
#       then: node --experimental-sqlite opencode.mjs --version  (stock Node 22.9.0)
#       Evidence and host smoke matrix: docs/OPENCODE_BUILD.md
# Status: required for the iPhoneOS bundle; the unpatched desktop Node build is unchanged.

